{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Uses a helper function _reverse_number to get the reverse of the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _reverse_number(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to reverse an integer, handling signs and trailing zeros.\"\"\"\n        sign = -1 if n < 0 else 1\n        n = abs(n)\n        reversed_n = 0\n        while n > 0:\n            digit = n % 10\n            reversed_n = reversed_n * 10 + digit\n            n //= 10\n        return reversed_n * sign\n\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number(number)\n    return number == (2 * reversed_num) - 1"}
