{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def max_difference(data: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements of pairs in a list of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains two numerical elements (int or float).\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum absolute difference found. Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any element within a pair is not a number or if a list item is not a tuple of two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0.0\n\n    for i, pair in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(pair, tuple) or len(pair) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid item at index {i}: Expected a tuple of two elements, got {type(pair).__name__} with {len(pair) if isinstance(pair, tuple) else 'N/A'} elements.\")\n\n        elem1, elem2 = pair\n\n        if not isinstance(elem1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(elem2, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid elements in pair at index {i}: Expected numbers, got ({type(elem1).__name__}, {type(elem2).__name__}).\")\n\n        current_diff = abs(float(elem1) - float(elem2))\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n\n    return max_diff"}
